<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">The Premise</span>
  <h2>What "AI in Agriculture" Actually Means</h2>
  <p class="lead" style="max-width: 820px;">
    AI in agriculture is the application of machine learning, computer vision, and data systems to
    farming and the wider agrifood chain — from a seedling in a nursery to produce on a shelf. It spans
    precision agriculture, autonomous machinery, post-harvest quality control, yield forecasting, and
    the policy that decides who benefits from all of it.
  </p>
  <p style="max-width: 820px; color: var(--muted);">
    Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko is an AI in agriculture educator, author, and speaker who works at exactly that
    intersection — technical innovation, public policy, and commercial viability. The throughline of this
    work is human-first: technology should widen access for smallholders and specialists alike, not just
    optimise the largest operations.
  </p>

