<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">Questions, Answered</span>
  <h2>AI in Agriculture FAQ</h2>
  <div style="display: grid; gap: 20px; max-width: 860px; margin-top: 30px;">

    <div class="card">
      <h3>What is AI in agriculture?</h3>
      <p>AI in agriculture is the use of machine learning, computer vision, and data systems across farming and the agrifood chain — including precision agriculture, autonomous machinery, post-harvest quality control, yield forecasting, and supply-chain optimisation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Is the AI in Agriculture course free?</h3>
      <p>Yes. <em>AI in Agriculture: Practical Introductory Course</em> is free to enrol on <a class="text-link" href="https://aiinagriculture.org/courses/ai-in-agriculture/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aiinagriculture.org</a>: 15 video lessons (1h 14m) and 8 quizzes, marked server-side, with a certificate anyone can verify. No technical background is required. 80:20, the monthly report, is £1 a month by subscription.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Who is Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko?</h3>
      <p>Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko is a UK-based AI in agriculture educator, author, and speaker, and a LinkedIn Top Voice on the subject. She teaches a course on AI in agriculture reaching {{ stats.udemy }} students across {{ stats.countries }} countries, and wrote The Precision Vineyard, a grower's field guide to AI, sensors and robotics. She won the Innovate UK Women in Innovation Award 2026 for MooMore, which detects inflammation in dairy cows before lameness becomes visible.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>What are the main applications of AI in agriculture?</h3>
      <p>The most established applications are precision agriculture, computer-vision quality control for produce and nursery stock, predictive analytics for yield and risk, autonomous machinery, and decision support that helps growers reduce waste while improving output.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Where can I learn about AI in agriculture?</h3>
      <p>Start with the free course on <a class="text-link" href="https://aiinagriculture.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aiinagriculture.org</a>, then subscribe to 80:20 for a monthly read on what changed. You can also follow the AI in Agriculture newsletter on <a class="text-link" href="{{ site.social.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>, watch explainers on <a class="text-link" href="{{ site.social.youtube }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube</a>, or read The Precision Vineyard. For organisations, a guest lecture or workshop is the usual route.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Has Maryna Kuzmenko written a book on AI in agriculture?</h3>
      <p>Yes. She writes the AI in Agriculture series: <em>The Precision Vineyard: A Grower's Field Guide to AI, Sensors and Robotics</em> (book 1) covers what to adopt, what to skip, and what it pays back in viticulture, and <em>Seed Quality Control</em> (book 2) is a practical guide to imaging and automation in vegetable seed. She also wrote <em>Vertical Farming: A Guide for Growing Minds</em>. See the <a class="text-link" href="/books/">books page</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>How can I book Maryna to speak on AI in agriculture?</h3>
      <p>Visit the <a class="text-link" href="/speaking/">speaking page</a> to see signature topics and formats, then use the <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">contact page</a> to check availability for your event.</p>
    </div>

  </div>
